<article>
	<div class="intro">
		<h1>Websites</h1>
		<p class="lede"><span class="gradient-text">You get a finished website that looks like you</span>. You can keep it without me.</p>

		<p>I make websites for small businesses, artists, authors, and people who need a clear page on the web. Not a theme you fight. Not a monthly retainer.</p>

		<p>We write the words together, in a short organized pass, not a month of revisions. You edit the site later in Sanity, which is built for that. When we launch, the site is yours. I am optional after that.</p>
	</div>

	<div class="what-happens">
	<h2>What happens</h2>
	<ol class="steps">
		<li>
			<p class="step-when">Before</p>
			<h3>Intake: who you are, what the site has to do, what <em>done</em> looks like</h3>
			<p>A short written brief — pages, tone, and what we will not build</p>
		</li>
		<li>
			<p class="step-when">Build</p>
			<h3>We write together, then I ship the site</h3>
			<p>A live site that looks like you. As little as 3 weeks</p>
		</li>
		<li>
			<p class="step-when">Handoff</p>
			<h3>How to edit in Sanity, what to do when you want a change</h3>
			<p>You can keep it. I am optional.</p>
		</li>
	</ol>
	</div>

	<aside class="fit">
		<h2 class="sr-only">Are we a fit?</h2>
		<section>
			<h3>Good fit</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>A small business, artist, author, or person who needs a real site (portfolio, shop-window, “this is me”)</li>
				<li>You will work with me on the words. I will keep that part tight</li>
				<li>You want to own the site and edit it yourself</li>
				<li>One finished site — not an ongoing marketing program</li>
				<li>You can be anywhere. Intake is a call or, if you are local, in person</li>
			</ul>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h3>Not this</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>WordPress</li>
				<li>A custom store built from scratch (Shopify is fine if that is the right tool)</li>
				<li>A theme you will “just tweak”</li>
				<li>A monthly retainer to keep improving it</li>
				<li>Ads, or “make us go viral”</li>
				<li>A large-company redesign, or a site that needs a team</li>
			</ul>
		</section>
	</aside>

	<section class="faq">
		<h2>Questions</h2>
		<details name="faq">
			<summary>Who is this for?</summary>
			<p>You need a real site, not a social profile. Remote is fine. If you already know what the site is <em>for</em>, we can talk.</p>
		</details>
		<details name="faq">
			<summary>What do I actually get?</summary>
			<p>The live site, the copy we wrote, and Sanity set up so you can edit pages yourself. I keep the writing organized so we are not trading drafts forever.</p>
		</details>
		<details name="faq">
			<summary>How long does it take?</summary>
			<p>As little as 3 weeks. Most of that is the writing pass and your feedback.</p>
		</details>
		<details name="faq">
			<summary>Do I have to be in New York?</summary>
			<p>No. Remote is fine. If you are in the NY Metro area we can meet in person for intake. We do not need to sit in a room for the whole build.</p>
		</details>
		<details name="faq">
			<summary>Do you work in WordPress? Can you build a shop?</summary>
			<p>No WordPress. I will not build a custom store from scratch. Shopify is fine if you need that. I can do basic SEO if you want it. I will not sell you an SEO retainer.</p>
		</details>
		<details name="faq">
			<summary>Will you just keep the site forever?</summary>
			<p>No. Handoff includes a walkthrough. If you want a later change, we can talk about that as a new, small thing.</p>
		</details>
		<details name="faq">
			<summary>How much does it cost?</summary>
			<p>Usually $2,500–$6,000 for a typical site. It can vary with how many pages, how much we write together, and whether we are replacing something messy.</p>
		</details>
		<details name="faq">
			<summary>How do we start?</summary>
			<p>Message me on LinkedIn with what the site is for and a link to anything you have now (even if you hate it). We’ll see if it’s a fit.</p>
		</details>
	</section>

